{"type":"assistant","uuid":"5a53362d-dfb3-40af-96bd-76c68f1e57f1","session_id":"f10e3351-58dd-4e3f-89b0-26388e1fd132","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"5a53362d-dfb3-40af-96bd-76c68f1e57f1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The exploration agent found the issue. The root cause is in `Whiteboard.drawFinish()` - it only calls `supportInvalidateOptionsMenu()` when `mUndo.size() == 1` (i.e., only on the first stroke). After erasing all drawings, when the user redraws, the first stroke will have `mUndo.size() == 1`, which should trigger the menu invalidation. But the issue is that the menu needs to be invalidated for EVERY stroke, not just the first one, because the button needs to change from disabled to enabled state.\n\nLet me read the actual source code to understand this better and confirm the fix.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
